      "text": "We are given that the equations $2x + 7 = 3$ and $bx - 10 = -2$ have the same solution $x$. To find the value of $b$, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Solve the first equation: $2x + 7 = 3$\n2. Use the solution for $x$ from the first equation to substitute into the second equation and solve for $b$.\n\nLet's start with the first equation:\n\n\\[ 2x + 7 = 3 \\]\n\nSubtract 7 from both sides to isolate the term with $x$:\n\n\\[ 2x + 7 - 7 = 3 - 7 \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[ 2x = -4 \\]\n\nNow, divide both sides by 2 to solve for $x$:\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{-4}{2} \\]\n\n\\[ x = -2 \\]\n\nSo, the solution to the first equation $2x + 7 = 3$ is $x = -2$. \n\nNext, we substitute $x = -2$ into the second equation $bx - 10 = -2$:\n\n\\[ b(-2) - 10 = -2 \\]\n\nDistribute $b$:\n\n\\[ -2b - 10 = -2 \\]\n\nAdd 10 to both sides to isolate the term with $b$:\n\n\\[ -2b - 10 + 10 = -2 + 10 \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[ -2b = 8 \\]\n\nNow, divide both sides by -2 to solve for $b$:\n\n\\[ b = \\frac{8}{-2} \\]\n\n\\[ b = -4 \\]\n\nSo, the value of $b$ is \\boxed{-4}.",
