      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the value of \\( b \\) for which the equations \\( 2x + 7 = 3 \\) and \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\) have the same solution \\( x \\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Solve the first equation for \\( x \\).\n2. Substitute the value of \\( x \\) into the second equation to solve for \\( b \\).\n\nLet's proceed with the calculations step-by-step using Python code.\n\n### Step 1: Solve the first equation for \\( x \\)\n\n\\[\n2x + 7 = 3\n\\]\n\nSubtract 7 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n2x = 3 - 7\n\\]\n\\[\n2x = -4\n\\]\n\nNext, divide both sides by 2:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-4}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\nx = -2\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the second equation and solve for \\( b \\)\n\nGiven the second equation:\n\n\\[\nbx - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( x = -2 \\):\n\n\\[\nb(-2) - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nMultiply out:\n\n\\[\n-2b - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nAdd 10 to both sides:\n\n\\[\n-2b = -2 + 10\n\\]\n\\[\n-2b = 8\n\\]\n\nFinally, divide both sides by -2:\n\n\\[\nb = \\frac{8}{-2}\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -4\n\\]\n\nLet's verify these steps with Python code to ensure the calculations are correct.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the variables\nx, b = symbols('x b')\n\n# Define the equations\neq1 = Eq(2*x + 7, 3)\neq2 = Eq(b*x - 10, -2)\n\n# Solve eq1 for x\nx_value = solve(eq1, x)[0]\n\n# Substitute x_value into eq2 and solve for b\nb_value = solve(eq2.subs(x, x_value), b)[0]\nprint(b_value)\n```\n```output\n-4\n```\nThe value of \\( b \\) for which the equations \\( 2x + 7 = 3 \\) and \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\) have the same solution \\( x \\) is \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-4}\n\\]",
